    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The linked PR fills in what the one-line note leaves out. [ev-60106c37139b] says a Usage in a namespace is now rejected if it has no `by` resource and specifies a namespace for its `of` resource. This holds even when that namespace is the Usage's own, because the check cannot read the object's namespace [ev-1d8a632a6ff4]. [ev-f9fa4bab35bc] shows the rule lives in the protection.crossplane.io v1beta1 Usage type and its CRD schema, with e2e tests for invalid cross-namespace ref and selector cases. Together these give the subject (the namespaced protection Usage resource), the change (a new validation rule), who is exposed (Usages that set `of` with a namespace but no `by`) and the consequence (the API server rejects them).",
